      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Catalyst::Plugin::Authentication versions before 0.10029 for Perl allow timing attacks on stored passwords via eq comparisons in the legacy password verifier.\n\nCVE-2026-5091 was fixed in the realm-based verifier. The legacy verifier, used by the deprecated login method, compares clear-text passwords, crypt hashes and base64 digests with eq, so the comparison time depends on how many leading bytes match.\n\nA remote attacker can use response-time differences to guess the stored password or hash.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
